WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200
So there's two options ahead of you.

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.040
Do you agree?

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:02.880
This is important.

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:03.700
Do you agree?

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.120
So is Donald Trump, okay, let me ask a question back

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:05.960
because you're asking me questions.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.280
You're not answering the basic point.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.200
Do you think Donald Trump is dismantling the Constitution?

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.040
Can we agree that Donald Trump is dismantling it?

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:11.880
Because I'll agree with you on that.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.080
I think he is dismantling the Constitution.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:13.900
I think he's-

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:14.740
Illegally, unconstitutionally, undemocratic.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.120
I think he's interpreting it in ways that are more-

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.559
Which judges do not agree with him on.

00:00:18.559 --> 00:00:19.400
Okay, hold on.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:20.719
Which the Supreme Court has not agreed with him on.

00:00:20.719 --> 00:00:21.719
And the judges don't agree

00:00:21.719 --> 00:00:23.799
with the people who wrote the Constitution.

00:00:23.799 --> 00:00:24.799
How do you know that?

00:00:24.799 --> 00:00:27.799
Okay, let's take your example of the Second Amendment.

00:00:27.799 --> 00:00:28.639
Let's say that a bunch of judges-

00:00:28.639 --> 00:00:29.719
I didn't give the Second Amendment.

00:00:29.719 --> 00:00:30.559
No, no, no, hold on, hold on, hold on.

00:00:30.559 --> 00:00:31.379
I said first, fourth,

00:00:31.379 --> 00:00:32.220
you don't want to talk about the ones I've given.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.060
No, you're interrupting me, you're interrupting me.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:33.880
Let me say them one more time.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:34.720
Because you're ignoring me.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.799
First, fourth, fifth, 14th, 22nd Amendments.

00:00:37.799 --> 00:00:39.119
Those are my amendments that I came with today.

00:00:39.119 --> 00:00:39.959
I'm trying-

00:00:39.959 --> 00:00:40.880
If you don't want to debate them, just say so.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.860
I'm trying to understand your ideology.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.840
You believe that dismantling the Constitution is okay-

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:47.680
You won't talk about the first, fourth, fifth, 14th,

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.520
22nd Amendments.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:49.340
When it's about parts of the Constitution

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.180
that you disagree with.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.000
You would be fine getting rid of the Second Amendment

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.599
but that would be a dismantling of the Constitution.

00:00:52.599 --> 00:00:54.200
No, because it would be done via Constitution.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.799
It means I'm not the one sitting here like your pal-

00:00:56.799 --> 00:00:57.639
You have agreed.

00:00:57.639 --> 00:00:58.480
You have agreed the Constitution-

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.200
I'm not the one saying you just get rid of them

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.040
willy-nilly.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:01.860
I don't agree.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:02.700
We're ramping up, we're ramping up.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.000
I don't agree that Joe Biden should come in

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.440
and say by executive order,

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.279
if Joe Biden put out an executive order saying

00:01:08.279 --> 00:01:10.080
Second Amendment no longer applies,

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.959
I can round up everyone's guns.

00:01:11.959 --> 00:01:12.800
I don't agree with that.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:13.620
Your result is exactly the same.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:14.459
I don't agree with them.

00:01:14.459 --> 00:01:15.800
No, but I don't agree with the method of doing it.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:16.639
It's unconstitutional.

00:01:16.639 --> 00:01:17.459
That's fine.

00:01:17.459 --> 00:01:18.959
He would have been defying the Constitution

00:01:18.959 --> 00:01:19.800
and I would have said so

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:22.879
We've been sitting here for several minutes.

00:01:22.879 --> 00:01:24.760
All of your friends have seen me ask you several times.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:25.919
Do you agree that Donald Trump is defying

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:28.360
the first, fourth, fifth, 14th

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:29.760
and possibly 22nd amendments?

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.599
Your colleague at least admitted

00:01:31.599 --> 00:01:32.440
that he's defying the First Amendment.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.279
I understand that you came in here.

00:01:34.279 --> 00:01:35.720
What you are attempting to do

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.080
is simply frame this conversation

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:39.279
like you did with the first claim about Donald Trump.

00:01:39.279 --> 00:01:41.260
But then when anybody asks you any kind of question

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:42.599
that presses you to the least degree about-

00:01:42.599 --> 00:01:43.440
No, I answered.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.279
I said I would dismantle the Constitution

00:01:44.279 --> 00:01:45.919
but I would do it constitutionally,

00:01:45.919 --> 00:01:47.160
not by executive order.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.040
What I'm trying to get to

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.680
is to prove to everybody who's watching

00:01:49.699 --> 00:01:51.519
that what you care about is not the Constitution

00:01:51.519 --> 00:01:53.279
in what it represents or creates.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.919
You care about the Constitution

00:01:54.919 --> 00:01:56.199
only in so far as it allows you

00:01:56.199 --> 00:01:57.680
to achieve your political worldview.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:58.760
We agree on that.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.680
No, I care about the Constitution

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:02.760
because I don't think presidents should be

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:06.279
fascist dictators and violate the Constitution.

00:02:06.279 --> 00:02:07.120
That's what I'm saying.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:07.959
You care-

00:02:07.959 --> 00:02:08.779
And he is defying-

00:02:08.779 --> 00:02:09.619
I don't think the President should have the power

00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:11.320
to lock you and me up if we write an op-ed

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:12.160
that he doesn't like.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:12.979
That's awesome, I agree.

00:02:12.979 --> 00:02:14.020
I don't think the President should be able

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:16.600
to crack down on us if you and I decide to go protest

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:17.600
outside his parade.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:18.440
I agree with you.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:19.259
I don't think the President should be able

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:20.639
to deprive you and I of due process

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:22.100
or come into our homes without a warrant.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:22.940
And I think-

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:23.759
Well, let's end on agreement then.

00:02:23.759 --> 00:02:24.600
All right, pause.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:25.440
You've been voted out.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:26.259
I'm glad we ended on agreement.

00:02:26.259 --> 00:02:27.100
It's good to meet you.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.940
Good to meet you, Kai.

